00:00:00.069 --> 00:00:04.618
Hello everyone welcome to the laing focus channel and my name is paul

00:00:06.009 --> 00:00:11.459
what should i talk about today maybe i should talk about a language spoken by tens of millions of people

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:17.549
maybe i should talk about one of the world's major language families or a country with stunning linguistic diversity

00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:19.470
Mmm, no

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:24.510
I think today i'll talk about something a little different today's topic is toki epona

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.779
toki poni what's that toki poni is a

00:00:28.269 --> 00:00:34.589
constructed language meaning that it did not arise naturally but it was created by someone in order to fulfill certain

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:42.419
criteria or a certain vision the most well-known constructed language might be esperanto which i made a video about a couple of years ago

00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:47.850
Toki poni is another constructed language that i thought was unique and interesting enough to make a video about

00:00:48.070 --> 00:00:51.989
It's not spoken by very many people but it's well known amongst fans of

00:00:52.090 --> 00:00:59.279
constructed languages the name toki ponent means the language of good and as a minimalist language the idea behind it is

00:00:59.530 --> 00:01:00.940
extreme simplicity

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:02.890
especially in its core vocabulary

00:01:02.890 --> 00:01:05.610
the purpose of toki poni is not just to simplify

00:01:06.070 --> 00:01:11.070
communication but to simplify your own thinking to force yourself to eliminate unnecessary information

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:16.619
and ideas and focus on what's really important toki poni has a core vocabulary of only

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:20.009
123 words yes you heard that right

00:01:21.369 --> 00:01:26.639
123 words you can learn those hundred and twenty-three words in just a couple of hours using an app like

00:01:26.890 --> 00:01:31.619
memorize or unki i should point out that in its original form toki poni had just

00:01:32.170 --> 00:01:38.159
120 words but it seems that since then a few new words have come into common use amongst the toki puna community

00:01:38.470 --> 00:01:45.299
toki puna draws its vocabulary from a number of languages including english tok piscine finnish georgian dutch

00:01:45.790 --> 00:01:47.200
acadian french

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:55.079
Esperanto croatian and mandarin and cantonese and it's intended to be equally as easy to learn for people from all cultures and linguistic backgrounds

00:01:55.810 --> 00:02:00.390
the languages phonology is also very simple there are just nine consonants and

00:02:00.670 --> 00:02:06.030
there are five vowels there are no diphthong and there are no consonant clusters and

00:02:06.310 --> 00:02:12.929
every syllable ends in a vowel or in a nasal sound if we look at one toki poni word we can see how the simple

00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:18.989
phonology determines how the words were formed the word for sweet is suey the consonant cluster

00:02:19.209 --> 00:02:27.149
Sw schwa is not allowed so while vowel is inserted between the two consonants and the final t consonant 2 is also not allowed

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:29.250
this might seem kind of strange

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:32.579
But having these limitations makes toki poni words simple to pronounce

00:02:33.010 --> 00:02:37.890
Now the big question on everyone's mind is probably how the heck do you communicate using only

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:45.119
123 words well those 123 words usually cover a range of related meanings so there's ambiguity

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:53.129
Context helps you understand which meaning is being used for example the word coûte means ear but it also means to hear

00:02:53.319 --> 00:02:55.559
Listen pay attention to or obey

00:02:56.650 --> 00:03:00.989
Makuta a kalama mu c the sentence means on listening to music

00:03:01.239 --> 00:03:08.189
Here we know coûte is a verb because it comes after a pronoun which seems like the subject and it's followed by a direct object

00:03:08.409 --> 00:03:11.189
marker a which itself is one of the

00:03:11.739 --> 00:03:16.139
123 words of toki bona and out of the several possible meanings for this verb

00:03:16.390 --> 00:03:19.049
listen makes the most sense in this context as

00:03:19.209 --> 00:03:26.789
For the word meaning music we'll come back to that in a minute another example the word moku means food or eat or drink

