So does the verb mean eat or drink

00:03:47.099 --> 00:03:54.029
Well you don't eat water so obviously it means drink so the sentence means you are drinking water or you drink water

00:03:54.910 --> 00:03:56.910
another example the word celie

00:03:57.280 --> 00:04:04.679
means warm as an adjective but also warmth or heat as a noun and also warm or heat as a verb

00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:13.079
sally sue no lisa lea, tomomi the warmth of the sun heats my home word for word this sentences warmth son

00:04:13.690 --> 00:04:17.279
subject marker heats direct object marker house

00:04:17.620 --> 00:04:24.239
my in the first case here celie is a noun because it comes before another noun you can imagine the word of

00:04:24.550 --> 00:04:30.900
between them if sally came after the suno then it would be the adjective warm this word li is a

00:04:31.030 --> 00:04:37.950
subject marker and i'll talk more about that in a minute here celie is a verb because it's followed by the direct object marker

00:04:38.430 --> 00:04:44.940
this word tomo is used for house but also has the more general meaning of structure and can mean building etc

00:04:45.130 --> 00:04:52.950
So the subject marker li is placed after subjects aside from me meaning i and sina the singular form of you

00:04:53.290 --> 00:04:56.159
without that word li to clearly mark the subject

00:04:56.320 --> 00:05:03.809
sentences could get confusing like in this case the verb cellie might be heard as an adjective if it comes directly after the word sunol

00:05:04.660 --> 00:05:12.480
so you can see that context both in situation and in syntax helps us to deal with ambiguity and understand which meaning is intended

